r, sponsorship has become a vital aspect of a team's survival. A youth team must have a sponsor, otherwise, their club will face disbandment, and are not permitted to partake in matches.\n\nThe series focuses on the forward Asuto Inamori and his team, Inakuni Raimon, which is made up of players from the remote Inakunijima Island. They have replaced the original Raimon Eleven as Raimon Junior High's soccer team, and are competing as underdogs in the annual Football Frontier youth tournament.\n\n(Source: Wikpedia)"},"tags":[{"name":"Football","rank":100,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Super Power","rank":84,"spoiler":false},{"name":"School Club","rank":79,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Primarily Male Cast","rank":79,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Ensemble Cast","rank":79,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Kids","rank":79,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Primarily Child Cast","rank":79,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Male Protagonist","rank":60,"spoiler":false}],"titles":{"display":"Inazuma Eleven Ares","english":"Inazuma Eleven Ares","native":"イナズマイレブン アレスの天秤","romaji":"Inazuma Eleven: Ares no Tenbin","synonyms":[{"language":"zh","source":"bangumi","value":"闪电十一人 阿瑞斯的天平"}]},"trailer":{"id":"wLFWgPe_GCc","site":"youtube","thumbnail":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/wLFWgPe_GCc/hqdefault.jpg"},"visibility":"general"}